WEBVTT

00:00:00.100 --> 00:00:04.398
Visible-light, or R G B, cameras support general condition documentation.

00:00:04.398 --> 00:00:06.547
Resolution, focus, dynamic range, stabilization,

00:00:06.547 --> 00:00:11.275
and lens quality affect whether small features remain useful after review.

00:00:11.275 --> 00:00:16.433
Zoom cameras can place more pixels on a target while maintaining standoff,

00:00:16.433 --> 00:00:20.731
but magnification also amplifies vibration, haze, atmospheric movement, focus error,

00:00:20.731 --> 00:00:22.021
and narrow framing.

00:00:22.021 --> 00:00:25.459
Capture wider reference images so close-ups remain locatable.

00:00:25.459 --> 00:00:29.757
Thermal sensors can reveal apparent temperature patterns for qualified review.

00:00:29.757 --> 00:00:33.196
Environment, material, emissivity, reflection, load, distance, angle, resolution,

00:00:33.196 --> 00:00:35.345
and calibration context affect interpretation.

00:00:35.345 --> 00:00:38.354
A color difference is not a diagnosis.

00:00:38.354 --> 00:00:41.363
Multispectral sensors can support specialized vegetation, environmental,

00:00:41.363 --> 00:00:44.371
or material workflows at a high level.

00:00:44.371 --> 00:00:46.520
They require mission-specific calibration, processing,

00:00:46.520 --> 00:00:52.108
and expertise and should not be selected simply because they collect more bands.

00:00:52.108 --> 00:00:54.257
Still images preserve discrete detail.

00:00:54.257 --> 00:00:56.406
Video supports movement, continuous context,

00:00:56.406 --> 00:01:01.564
and rapid coverage but may provide less per-frame quality and larger files.

00:01:01.564 --> 00:01:05.862
Use each format only when it helps the inspection question.

00:01:05.862 --> 00:01:09.731
Match sensor field of view, resolution, metadata, measurement capability,

00:01:09.731 --> 00:01:13.599
and payload weight to the target and required decision.

00:01:13.599 --> 00:01:18.327
The best payload is the one that produces defensible evidence safely,

00:01:18.327 --> 00:01:20.906
not the most complex sensor available.

00:01:20.906 --> 00:01:25.634
Verify the payload before mobilization with representative targets or approved checks.

00:01:25.634 --> 00:01:30.362
Confirm focus, storage, timestamp, metadata, stabilization, zoom behavior, thermal data format,

00:01:30.362 --> 00:01:34.660
and processing compatibility rather than discovering a mismatch after flight.
